{
  "method": "Writer: ordinary least squares of rss_kb (gauge, unlabeled series in metrics.jsonl) vs. wall-clock seconds since each life's first sample, split at the 3 recorded restart death timestamps in recoveries-4.jsonl (giving 4 lives). Reader (harness series): OLS of rss_kb (gauge, labels={'reader': idx}) vs. wall-clock seconds since the run's first sample, one fit per reader over its whole run (reader_restarts=0, so readers never restart and have a single life each); this is the same metrics.jsonl gauge the writer series uses, sampled on each reader's own query-loop cadence (~1362 points over the reader's ~86334.4s span, i.e. essentially the full 24h run) rather than on a fixed wall-clock tick. Reader (sampler/composition series): OLS of VmSize/VmRSS/RssAnon/RssFile (kB, from /proc/<pid>/status via the coordinator's independent sampler, copied verbatim to rss_composition-4.log) vs. wall-clock seconds since that pid's first sample in the log; rows with role='[_child ]' are excluded per the pre-registration (that role is a miscellaneous/unidentified child, not a reader or writer). The sampler log carries pid and role only, not the harness's own reader index; the 8 reader pids are mapped to idx 0..7 by ascending pid order, which matches both the spawn order (pids are assigned sequentially by the OS at fork time, lowest-to-highest in idx order) and watch.log's own per_child_rss listing, which enumerates the same 8 pids directly after the writer's pid at every 300s sample. This mapping is corroborative, not independently proven, but the resulting VmRSS/RssAnon/RssFile/VmSize slope ranges exactly reproduce the coordinator's own quoted ranges (VmRSS 5.85-6.45, RssAnon 4.81-5.41, RssFile 1.03-1.06, VmSize 6.62-7.17 kB/s) to within rounding, so a mislabeling would have to be a same-valued permutation to go undetected -- treated here as strong corroboration, not proof.",
  "frozen_bound_writer_kb_per_s": 50,
  "frozen_bound_reader_kb_per_s": 10,
  "frozen_bound_reader_pin_attributable_kb_per_s": 0.01,
  "pin_attribution_limit": "The pre-registration's clause (c) caps the pin-attributable part of the reader RSS slope at <=0.01 kB/s, distinct from VSZ (not scored). No pre-fix (i.e. D-088-broken-engine) file-backed RSS series exists for this store/config to difference against -- P-SOAK4 is the first run of the fixed engine, so there is no prior broken-engine sample at the same store size to isolate a 'pin' delta from. The composition series below (RssFile slope 1.03-1.06 kB/s across all 8 readers) shows file-backed memory growing slowly but non-trivially over 24h; whether any part of that is pin-attributable cannot be determined from these instruments (no before/after-fix pair, no pin-specific counter). This is stated plainly rather than guessed at: the pin-attributable clause of (c) is NOT CHECKED by this record, same category of honest limit as soak3's compaction-stall row.",
